  python3 tools/logprob_diff.py save NAME
  python3 tools/logprob_diff.py check NAME     # max/mean |dlogprob| vs NAME
  python3 tools/logprob_diff.py compare A B    # symmetric: B vs A

Teacher forcing (``logprob_start_len`` + a forced continuation) makes the
comparison independent of the decode path: it measures the prefill and the
first-step logits.  The continuation is fixed token ids from
``tools/greedy/oa.json`` (the same ids the greedy oracle uses), so the
comparison does not depend on the model's own decode.  The prompt is the same
determin"    LOGPROB_MAX={overall['max']:.6f} LOGPROB_MEAN={overall['mean']:.6f}")


def main() -> None:
    if len(sys.argv) < 2:
        print(__doc__)
        sys.exit(1)
    cmd = sys.argv[1]
    if cmd == "save":
        name = sys.argv[2]
        path = D / f"{name}.json"
        path.write_text(json.dumps(collect(), indent=2))
        print(f"  saved {path}")
    elif cmd == "check":
        ref = json.loads((D / f"{sys.argv[2]}.json").read_text())
        cur = collect(cached=ref)
        report = stats(ref, cur)
        print_report(f"{sys.argv[2]} vs current", report)
    elif cmd == "compare":
        a = json.loads((D / f"{sys.argv[2]}.json").read_text())
        b = json.loads((D / f"{sys.argv[3]}.json").read_text())
        print_report(f"{sys.argv[3]} vs {sys.argv[2]}", stats(a, b))
    else:
        print(__doc__)
        sys.exit(1)


if __name__ == "__main__":
    main()


